# Vercel Web Analytics Installation

Successfully installed and configured Vercel Web Analytics for the GamePulse project.

## Changes Made

### 1. Package Installation
- Installed `@vercel/analytics` version 2.0.1 using npm
- Package added to dependencies in package.json

### 2. Configuration
Modified `/app/layout.tsx`:
- Added import statement: `import { Analytics } from "@vercel/analytics/next";`
- Added `<Analytics />` component at the end of the body element in the root layout
- Follows Next.js App Router best practices by placing the component in the root layout

### 3. Files Modified
- `app/layout.tsx` - Added Analytics import and component
- `package.json` - Added @vercel/analytics dependency
- `package-lock.json` - Updated with new dependency information

## Implementation Details

The implementation follows the latest official Vercel Analytics documentation (fetched from https://vercel.com/docs/analytics/quickstart):
- Used the framework-specific Next.js App Router installation method
- Placed the Analytics component in the root layout within the body element
- This ensures analytics tracking across all pages of the application

## Build Verification

- ✅ Build completed successfully with `npm run build`
- ✅ TypeScript compilation passed without errors
- ✅ All pages generated correctly (34 routes total)
- ⚠️  ESLint warnings present but unrelated to this change (pre-existing issues in other files)

## Next Steps

To complete the setup, the project owner needs to:
1. Deploy the application to Vercel
2. Enable Web Analytics in the Vercel dashboard under the Analytics section
3. The Analytics feature will be active after the next deployment

## Notes

The Analytics component will automatically track page views and Web Vitals metrics. In development mode, it will not send data to Vercel. Analytics will only be active in production deployments on Vercel.
